From: LIVI <noreply@f-io.dev>
Subject: [PATCH] spi: spidev: allow a "livi,x1600-led" device

spidev refuses to bind to a compatible string it does not know, as a safety net against exposing a
device userspace should not poke directly. The vendor's own rootfs drives this board's RGB LED the
same way, over /dev/spidev0.0 (confirmed: `strings` on its colorLedSpi binary), so this is the same
trade ax520's own "ax520-led" entry already makes.
---
--- a/drivers/spi/spidev.c
+++ b/drivers/spi/spidev.c
@@ -690,6 +690,7 @@
 	{ .name = /* dh */ "dhcom-board" },
 	{ .name = /* elgin */ "jg10309-01" },
 	{ .name = /* gocontroll */ "moduline-module-slot"},
+	{ .name = /* livi */ "x1600-led" },
 	{ .name = /* lineartechnology */ "ltc2488" },
 	{ .name = /* lwn */ "bk4" },
 	{ .name = /* lwn */ "bk4-spi" },
@@ -724,6 +725,7 @@
 	{ .compatible = "dh,dhcom-board", .data = &spidev_of_check },
 	{ .compatible = "elgin,jg10309-01", .data = &spidev_of_check },
 	{ .compatible = "gocontroll,moduline-module-slot", .data = &spidev_of_check},
+	{ .compatible = "livi,x1600-led", .data = &spidev_of_check },
 	{ .compatible = "lineartechnology,ltc2488", .data = &spidev_of_check },
 	{ .compatible = "lwn,bk4", .data = &spidev_of_check },
 	{ .compatible = "lwn,bk4-spi", .data = &spidev_of_check },
